      "heading": "B — Audience and scope",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience and scope\n\nAudience: first-time Iowa license applicants learning the named signs they will meet on the road and on the test, working in plain English.\n\nPrerequisites: the color-and-shape code from the previous section is assumed; this section names the signs that use that code.\n\nScope note: named regulatory and warning signs only — what each sign orders or warns about and what to do. Signals, crossings, and lane markings live in later sections.\n\nVisual emphasis: candidates must name each sign and its required response at a glance, so this section feeds the dedicated sign-identification surface declared in part C.\n",
